<section class="page-head"><div class="container"><span class="status-pill">In progress</span><div class="eyebrow">Frontend · React · TypeScript · Vite</div><h1>Reel Good — Movie Discovery Web Application</h1><p class="section-lead">A user-facing movie discovery application being developed as part of the FlyRank frontend track.</p></div></section>
<section><div class="container content">
<section class="story-section"><h2>Project at a glance</h2><div class="story-grid"><div class="story-step"><strong>1 · Objective</strong><p>Build a usable frontend around live external movie data rather than a static interface.</p></div><div class="story-step"><strong>2 · Data</strong><p>Movie metadata returned by the OMDb API, supported by a small curated starter collection.</p></div><div class="story-step"><strong>3 · Method</strong><p>Use React, TypeScript and Vite for search, detail pages, routing and genre browsing, with Firebase architecture for authentication and favourites.</p></div><div class="story-step"><strong>4 · Evaluation</strong><p>Automated tests cover routing, live movie flows and account/favourites behaviour; final live Firebase verification remains outstanding.</p></div><div class="story-step story-impact"><strong>5 · Outcome</strong><p>The project demonstrates user-facing product development and external-API integration, but remains explicitly in progress until its remaining verification work is complete.</p></div></div></section>
<h2>Current implementation</h2>
<ul>
<li>React + TypeScript + Vite application architecture.</li>
<li>Live OMDb title search with pagination, loading, empty and error states, request cancellation and stale-response protection.</li>
<li>Movie detail pages, genre browsing, poster fallbacks and verified IMDb links.</li>
<li>Server-side OMDb proxy with caching, request limiting and bounded detail enrichment.</li>
<li>Firebase email/password authentication and UID-scoped favourites architecture.</li>
<li>Vitest and React Testing Library coverage for routing, live movie flows and authentication/favourites behaviour.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Current verification</h2>
<p>Automated frontend tests cover the major flows and the application is publicly previewable. OMDb integration, routing and core UI behaviour are implemented.</p>

<h2>Remaining work</h2>
<p>Firebase/live end-to-end verification, browser/mobile manual checks and later frontend-capstone work remain outstanding. The project is therefore intentionally separated from the completed case studies.</p>

